      "ratio": 2.1181872206246966,
      "max_ratio": null,
      "pass": true,
      "note": "the budget, the store's bounded index cache and overlay, and what stays resident by design: the wheel's pending decision per herd (about 40 bytes)"
    },
    {
      "sweep": "herds-paged",
      "model": "dyadic",
      "metric": "cpu_per_unit",
      "measured": 0.09089835678800831,
      "declared": 0.1,
      "scale_md": 0.0,
      "ratio": 1.2866266057552853,
      "max_ratio": 4.0,
      "pass": true,
      "note": "the same decisions as herds-wide, plus a page load per page of herds and forage a sub-season"
    },
    {
      "sweep": "factions-paged",
      "model": "closed",
      "metric": "resident",
      "measured": -0.0007179694417249489,
      "declared": 0.1,
      "scale_md": 0.0,
      "ratio": 1.0009958124808498,
      "max_ratio": 4.0,
      "pass": true,
      "note": "the conflict's row tables (factions with their feuds, sources, places) are held to the budget plus one step's changes whatever the faction count (A16): the host saves when every resident page is changed (Conflict::needs_save, PM-C10), so the saves a day grow with the factions instead (reported, saves_per_day). The phase 1 world under the camps is not paged here and is most of the heap, so the engine's own live bytes are reported apart (engine_live_bytes): about 580 bytes a faction stay resident by design (the wheel, parties in flight, the indexes: PM-C4, PM-C13)"
    },
